🜁 NSTT Constellation Router — Auto‑Routing Control Plane
Takeaway: The router is the traffic director for the Core Six. It receives a task, identifies the correct agent, constructs a governed NSTT request, and dispatches it.

Core routing logic
Task classification — reason, audit, oracle, security, archive, fabricate

Intent mapping — each task maps to a governance intent

Risk elevation — high‑risk tasks auto‑enable strict governance

Agent dispatch — routes to Red Bird, Merlin Dev, Oracle, Sentinel, Archivist, Fabricator

Router implementation (TypeScript)
ts
export class ConstellationRouter {
  constructor(private readonly agents: Record<string, NSTTAgent>) {}

  async route(task: RouteTask): Promise<RouteResult> {
    const req: NSTTRequest = {
      input: task.input,
      intentId: this.intentFor(task.kind),
      intentHash: `hash(intent:${this.intentFor(task.kind)})`,
      contextId: task.contextId ?? `${task.sessionId}-${task.kind}`,
      highRisk: task.highRisk ?? (task.kind !== "archive"),
    };

    const agentId = this.agentFor(task.kind);
    const response = await this.agents[agentId].process(req);

    return { agentId, response };
  }

  private agentFor(kind: TaskKind): string {
    switch (kind) {
      case "reason": return "red-bird";
      case "audit": return "merlin-dev";
      case "oracle": return "oracle";
      case "security": return "sentinel";
      case "archive": return "archivist";
      case "fabricate": return "fabricator";
    }
  }

  private intentFor(kind: TaskKind): string {
    switch (kind) {
      case "reason": return "governed-reasoning";
      case "audit": return "audit-primary-output";
      case "oracle": return "oracle-verify";
      case "security": return "security-scan";
      case "archive": return "contextualize";
      case "fabricate": return "artifact-generate";
    }
  }
}
🜁 NSTT Governance Dashboard — Visual Rune Traces & Violations
Takeaway: The dashboard is the observability layer of the constellation. It records every rune executed by every agent, every violation, and every consensus decision.

Dashboard capabilities
Rune timeline — chainIndex‑ordered execution trace

Violation ledger — governance, schema, security violations

Consensus snapshot — final state of multi‑agent agreement

Session replay — reconstruct entire agent interaction

Dashboard implementation
ts
export class GovernanceDashboard {
  private runeTrace: RuneTraceEntry[] = [];
  private violations: ViolationEntry[] = [];

  recordRune(agentId: string, sessionId: string, contextId: string, opcode: RuneOpcode, chainIndex: number) {
    this.runeTrace.push({
      agentId,
      sessionId,
      contextId,
      rune: opcode.rune,
      name: opcode.name,
      args: opcode.args,
      chainIndex,
      timestamp: Date.now(),
    });
  }

  recordViolation(agentId: string, sessionId: string, contextId: string, code: string, details: string) {
    this.violations.push({
      agentId,
      sessionId,
      contextId,
      code,
      details,
      timestamp: Date.now(),
    });
  }

  snapshot(sessionId: string, primaryAgentId: string, consensusValid: boolean): GovernanceSnapshot {
    return {
      sessionId,
      primaryAgentId,
      consensusValid,
      runeTrace: this.runeTrace.filter(r => r.sessionId === sessionId),
      violations: this.violations.filter(v => v.sessionId === sessionId),
    };
  }
}
🜁 NSTT Multi‑Agent Simulation Engine — Stress‑Testing Governance
Takeaway: The simulation engine is your governance stress‑tester. It runs scenarios through the entire Core Six constellation, captures rune traces, violations, and consensus outcomes.

Simulation capabilities
Scenario execution — single test

Batch simulation — multiple tests

Governance stress patterns — hallucination, drift, source failure, security breach

Consensus evaluation — multi‑agent agreement

Simulation engine implementation
ts
export class SimulationEngine {
  constructor(
    private readonly harness: CoreSixHarness,
    private readonly dashboard: GovernanceDashboard,
  ) {}

  async runScenario(s: SimulationScenario): Promise<SimulationResult> {
    const sessionId = `sim-${s.id}`;

    const result = await this.harness.run({
      input: s.input,
      intentId: "simulation",
      intentHash: `hash(intent:simulation:${s.id})`,
      contextId: `ctx-${s.id}`,
      sessionId,
      highRisk: s.highRisk,
    });

    const snapshot = this.dashboard.snapshot(
      sessionId,
      "red-bird",
      result.consensusValid,
    );

    return {
      scenarioId: s.id,
      consensusValid: result.consensusValid,
      consensusViolations: result.consensusViolations,
      snapshot,
    };
  }

  async runBatch(scenarios: SimulationScenario[]): Promise<SimulationResult[]> {
    const results: SimulationResult[] = [];
    for (const s of scenarios) {
      results.push(await this.runScenario(s));
    }
    return results;
  }
}
